The pad's menu pointer (game/pad.cpp): the right stick steers the original's analog menu cursor, and the left stick,
which the original added to it, moves the keyboard focus instead. The cursor answers the stick quadratically, fine near
the centre and across the screen in about a second at full tilt, where the original's linear 540 units a second at the
default sensitivity took five. Moving the mouse hands the cursor back to it, where the original kept the stick's until
the next run. Only the mouse's own motion does: the client sends motion every frame to bring the game's cursor to the
window's (client/main.cpp), which the original took for the mouse moving and so dropped the stick's cursor at once.
